{"slug": "half-adder-vs-full-adder", "question": "What Is the Difference Between Half Adder and Full Adder?", "body_html": "<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">A half adder adds two bits, A and B, while a full adder adds three bits, A, B and a carry in from the previous stage.</p><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:8px 0 4px;font-size:16px;\"><tr style=\"background:#1a2b4a;color:#fff;\"><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Point</th><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Half Adder</th><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Full Adder</th></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Inputs</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">2 (A, B)</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">3 (A, B, Cin)</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#fff\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Sum</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">A XOR B</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">A XOR B XOR Cin</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Carry</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">A AND B</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Majority of A, B, Cin</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#fff\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Gates</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">1 XOR, 1 AND</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">2 XOR, 2 AND, 1 OR</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Cascading</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Cannot be chained</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Forms a ripple carry adder</td></tr></table>"}